<title>FRANCE: LVMH down on DFS unit profit worry.</title>
<headline>LVMH down on DFS unit profit worry.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French luxury goods group LVMH fell 3.78 percent on market talk that profits at its U.S. unit DFS Group Ltd -- Duty Free Shoppers -- in which it holds 61.25 percent, could fall 15 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>No immediate comment was available from the group.</p>
<p>At 1041 GMT, LVMH shares were down 53 francs at 1,350 francs in volume of 179,737 shares traded.</p>
<p>Traders linked the possible fall in profits to a drop in Japanese consumption triggered by a stronger dollar against the yen.</p>
</text>
